<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - S.AFRICA MAY PPI UP 0.9 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE - S.AFRICA MAY PPI UP 0.9 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities</p>
<p>producer price index rose 0.9 percent in May from April after</p>
<p>rising 0.4 percent in April, Central Statistical Service figures</p>
<p>show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in May was 8.4 percent after April's</p>
<p>8.8 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would</p>
<p>rise 0.8 percent month-on-month and 8.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 May'97   Apr'97   May'96    - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    8.4	 8.8     5.8	    0.9	0.4</p>
<p>Locally produced   8.9	 9.7     6.3	    0.4	1.2</p>
<p>Imported	     6.4	 5.4     4.6	    2.7     -3.2</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 May'97    Apr'97    May'96</p>
<p>All commodities    114.3     113.3     105.4</p>
<p>Locally produced   115.4     114.9     106.0</p>
<p>Imported	     110.5     107.6     103.9</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
